.TH KERN 1 "2025-11-03" "kern" "System Monitoring Tool"
.SH NAME
kern \- real-time system monitoring tool with REST API and remote monitoring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kern
[\-acdhmnv] [\-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR] [\-l \fILANG\fR] [\-r \fIPORT\fR] [\-\-detailed]
.B kern
[\-\-ssh \fIHOST\fR] [\-\-api \fIURL\fR] [\-\-download-lang \fICODE\fR] [\-\-list-languages]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kern
is a comprehensive system monitoring tool that provides real-time information
about disk usage, CPU performance, memory utilization, and network statistics.
It features a clean line-based interface with colored graphs, auto-refresh capabilities,
support for multiple languages with automatic download, and remote monitoring via
SSH and API.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show all system information (default).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cpu
Show CPU information only.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-disk
Show disk information only.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mem
Show memory information only.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-net
Show network information only.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR
Set refresh interval in seconds (default: 2).
.TP
.B \-l \fILANG\fR
Set interface language. Use \-\-list-languages to see all supported codes.
.TP
.B \-r \fIPORT\fR
Start remote API server on specified port.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Show detailed CPU core information (individual core usage).
.TP
.B \-\-ssh \fIHOST\fR
Monitor remote server via SSH (format: user@hostname).
.TP
.B \-\-api \fIURL\fR
Monitor remote server via API (format: http://hostname:port).
.TP
.B \-\-download-lang \fICODE\fR
Download language pack for specified language code.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
List all supported language codes.
.SH LANGUAGE SUPPORT
.B kern
supports over 50 languages. If a requested language is not available locally,
it can be automatically downloaded from the official repository.
.PP
Supported language groups include:
.IP \(bu 4
European languages (en, ru, es, fr, de, it, pt, nl, pl, sv, da, no, fi)
.IP \(bu 4
Eastern European languages (cs, hu, ro, bg, hr, sk, sl, et, lv, lt, uk, sr, bs, mk, sq, el)
.IP \(bu 4
Asian languages (ja, ko, zh, ar, hi, id, vi, th, tr, he, fa, ur, bn, ta, te, ml, kn, gu, mr, pa, ne)
.SH REMOTE MONITORING
.B kern
provides multiple methods for remote system monitoring:
.TP
.B API Monitoring
Start kern as an API server on the remote machine with
.B \-r
and connect from a client machine with
.B \-\-api.
.TP
.B SSH Monitoring
Monitor remote systems via SSH connection using
.B \-\-ssh
(planned feature).
.SH API
When started with the
.B \-r
option,
.B kern
provides a REST API on the specified port:
.TP
.B GET /api/cpu
Returns JSON with CPU information.
.TP
.B GET /api/mem
Returns JSON with memory information.
.TP
.B GET /api/disk
Returns JSON with disk information.
.TP
.B GET /api/net
Returns JSON with network information.
.TP
.B GET /api/system
Returns JSON with system information.
.TP
.B GET /health
Returns health status.
.PP
Example usage:
.IP
kern -r 8080
.br
curl http://localhost:8080/api/cpu
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B q
Quit the application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kern
Monitor all system resources with default settings.
.TP
.B kern \-d \-m
Monitor only disk and memory usage.
.TP
.B kern \-\-refresh=5 \-l ru
Update every 5 seconds with Russian interface.
.TP
.B kern \-\-detailed
Show detailed CPU core information.
.TP
.B kern \-r 8080
Start remote API server on port 8080.
.TP
.B kern \-\-ssh user@server
Monitor remote server via SSH.
.TP
.B kern \-\-api http://server:8080
Monitor remote server via API.
.TP
.B kern \-\-download-lang fr
Download French language pack.
.TP
.B kern \-\-list-languages
List all supported languages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kern/kern.json
Configuration file storing user preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kern/i18n/
Directory containing downloaded language packs.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/kern/i18n/
System directory containing language files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
